1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,609
Unit follows the apparatus context selected on this device,

2
00:00:03,769 --> 00:00:05,590
while a named person signs in.

3
00:00:05,909 --> 00:00:07,869
Identify both before working.

4
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:13,710
The active unit scopes status, roles, map context, routes, and inventory;

5
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:16,100
review it in Settings at each handoff.

6
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:20,200
This is useful for a SAR vehicle, community response

7
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,270
team, or industrial standby.

8
00:00:22,719 --> 00:00:27,049
A vehicle-mounted tablet still needs the correct member and apparatus selection.

9
00:00:27,229 --> 00:00:31,000
Use Next or Skip on the first-launch introduction,

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,149
then review Language

11
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,600
and Server URL on sign-in.

12
00:00:35,169 --> 00:00:38,729
Select the correct listed server or the permitted custom address

13
00:00:38,729 --> 00:00:40,319
before entering credentials.

14
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:44,120
The introduction describes features but does not prove every

15
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,630
device permission is granted.

16
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:49,960
Keep the server choice visible in the demonstration so a crew can recognize

17
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:53,560
a training environment and avoid confusing it with another deployment.

18
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:58,060
Use Username and Password and select Sign In for this training server.

19
00:00:58,489 --> 00:01:02,950
Sign in with SSO is an offered entry, but organization discovery and

20
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:05,299
provider callbacks are unverified here.

21
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,339
This lesson uses the ordinary credential flow.

22
00:01:08,719 --> 00:01:13,280
Additional verification depends on the methods the server offers; keep credential

23
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:17,509
entry private and check the resulting apparatus context before working.

24
00:01:17,730 --> 00:01:21,519
Choose Shared device when several members use the same installation.

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,619
Turn on This is a shared device and enter Device label (optional), such as the

26
00:01:27,619 --> 00:01:30,629
training apparatus identifier, then Save.

27
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:33,079
The setting takes effect at the next sign-in.

28
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:37,389
It identifies the installation; it does not turn a person’s credentials

29
00:01:37,389 --> 00:01:39,059
into a shared crew password.

30
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:43,380
Each member still follows the department’s session and verification policy.

31
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,410
Shared device identifies the saved installation.

32
00:01:46,809 --> 00:01:49,800
A normal reload in this exercise returned to Sign In.

33
00:01:50,270 --> 00:01:54,559
Follow the server’s supported sign-in procedure at handoff, verify the member,

34
00:01:54,809 --> 00:01:56,999
and recheck Active Unit before work.

35
00:01:57,410 --> 00:02:01,440
The label and sign-in boundary are demonstrated; shared-session locking,

36
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:05,979
unlocking, operator switching, and shift ending remain unverified.

37
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:09,069
Those branches require server-supported controls and

38
00:02:09,069 --> 00:02:10,880
permitted verification methods.

39
00:02:10,989 --> 00:02:15,229
In Settings, open Active Unit and choose the apparatus for this crew.

40
00:02:15,679 --> 00:02:19,539
Select Unit lists the units accessible to this member, and

41
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:21,699
Current Unit helps confirm the result.

42
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:25,649
If the expected unit is missing, ask an administrator to check

43
00:02:25,649 --> 00:02:26,990
station-group membership.

44
00:02:27,369 --> 00:02:31,009
Do not select a different vehicle merely to clear an empty state.

45
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:34,419
The selection scopes several operational screens and should

46
00:02:34,419 --> 00:02:35,929
be checked at every handoff.

47
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:38,000
Open the roles card and

48
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,509
inspect Unit Role Assignments.

49
00:02:39,919 --> 00:02:43,469
Officer / Team Lead already contains Christopher Herrmann.

50
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:46,779
Save is disabled because the roster has not changed.

51
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:49,930
The signed-in operator and assigned crew are separate.

52
00:02:50,330 --> 00:02:54,750
Review configured seats before an authorized crew change; role assignments

53
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:58,250
describe apparatus functions, while account permissions and dated

54
00:02:58,250 --> 00:02:59,860
shift sign-ups remain separate.

55
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:02,580
This exercise preserves Herrmann’s seat.

56
00:03:02,749 --> 00:03:05,170
The sidebar shows the active unit’s state.

57
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,000
A quick status button

58
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
opens that status’s destination or

59
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:09,799
note steps;

60
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:12,000
Set Active also opens

61
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:12,959
Select Status.

62
00:03:13,369 --> 00:03:15,699
This department uses ordinary Submit.

63
00:03:16,110 --> 00:03:20,199
Two-second holding and next-status restrictions depend on configuration.

64
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:22,000
Read the offered

65
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,330
destinations and note before submitting, then

66
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:26,090
confirm the saved unit state.

67
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:30,019
Unit status remains separate from the operator’s personal staffing.

68
00:03:30,299 --> 00:03:32,519
The call card shows the selected incident.

69
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,000
View Call

70
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,379
Details opens its full screen.

71
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:39,469
Directions offers a mapping handoff, which is unexercised here.

72
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:43,800
Deselect concerns app selection; incident closure is separate.

73
00:03:44,290 --> 00:03:47,000
Set Active selected our practice incident and

74
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,319
opened Select Status.

75
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:51,000
The unit’s response changed only after the

76
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,440
status submission, so verify selection

77
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:57,959
and response separately before describing the crew as dispatched or responding.

78
00:03:58,230 --> 00:04:00,000
Sign-in and security shows

79
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,979
Authenticator app, Passkeys for

80
00:04:01,979 --> 00:04:04,489
this app, and Recent verifications.

81
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:08,029
This account says no passkeys are registered for this app.

82
00:04:08,559 --> 00:04:12,580
This lesson inspects configuration and recovery prerequisites without

83
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:16,819
enrolling a method, replacing an authenticator, or changing credentials.

84
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:19,000
Login Info opens empty

85
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,600
Username and Password fields; Cancel

86
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,940
returns without saving.

87
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:26,000
Logout opens Confirm Logout;

88
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,819
Cancel preserves the current session.

